--- body ---
## Context

Child of 0193. That ticket's fix (PR pending) hardens the /verify
pipeline against fork drift: TASK DIRECTIVE openers, worktree= cwd
threading, an orchestrator-side containment postcondition, narrowed
erg-pr-merge staging, and a stash-discipline rule. The headline exit
criterion — one full raid cycle with zero off-task sub-skill runs and
zero foreign files — is empirical and cannot be proven by the PR that
ships the contracts. This ticket carries it.

Honesty note from the 0193 review: of the shipped fixes, only the
erg-pr-merge narrowing is mechanical. The TASK DIRECTIVE and the
worktree= cd both live *inside* the drift-prone fork — a fork that
ignores the directive ignores the cd too — and the postcondition
check is orchestrator-run, catching working-tree residue but not a
rogue push/PR (the #243 mode). `/simplify` is a built-in skill that
receives the worktree= hint in its args but carries no directive
contract. The 2026-06-03 evidence points at the deterministic
alternative: raid execute agents — `Agent(isolation:"worktree")`
with imperative prompts and pinned cwd — never drifted; only
`context: fork` Skill invocations did.

## Actions

1. Observe the next full raid cycle (or run one) with the 0193
   contracts in place. Audit every verify sub-skill transcript for
   off-task runs, foreign files, branch switches, rogue pushes/PRs.
2. If any drift recurs: convert /verify phases 2–4 and 6 from
   `context: fork` Skill invocations to `Agent`-spawned sub-agents
   with pinned cwd (the mechanism raid execute agents already use),
   or add a push/PR guard scoped to verify sub-skill sessions —
   whichever deterministically kills the #243 mode.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One full raid cycle with zero off-task sub-skill runs and zero
      foreign files in the orchestrator worktree after verify
- [ ] If drift recurred: the deterministic spawn fix (or guard) is
      ticketed or shipped